# =============================================================================
# .dockerignore — files Docker never sends into the build context
# =============================================================================
# WHAT: Same idea as .gitignore, but for "docker build" instead of "git add."
#       Anything matched here never leaves your machine when an image builds.
# WHY:  Without this, "docker build ." was uploading every local node_modules
#       folder into the build context, then each stage's "COPY server/ ./server/"
#       (and the same for client/) copied it straight into the image on top of
#       the node_modules that stage's own "npm ci" had just installed. Locally
#       built binaries like esbuild and lightningcss are platform-specific, so
#       a macOS node_modules copied into an Alpine Linux container can silently
#       replace a working Linux binary with one that won't run there. This file
#       existing at all is the fix, regardless of which patterns it lists.
# HOW:  Same glob syntax as .gitignore, evaluated relative to this directory.
# =============================================================================

node_modules
**/node_modules

dist
**/dist

.git
.gitignore

# Real secrets (.env) and per-environment templates (.env.dev/.env.staging/
# .env.prod) are handed to containers at runtime via docker-compose's
# "env_file:", never baked into an image layer.
.env
.env.dev
.env.staging
.env.prod
.env.local
.env.*.local

test-results
playwright-report
blob-report
coverage

*.log
.DS_Store
.idea
.vscode
